          "POB05P": "[{\"insert\":\"Brainstorming in text forces you to clearly articulate proposals, designs, and ideas, with less variance in interpretations. This also breaks down silos by making information easily accessible. Documentation also helps with transparency and fosters collaboration.\"}]",
          "78Nb1I": "[{\"insert\":\"Use indentations to organize the levels of information. In this way, your reader can easily zoom in / out.\"}]",
          "0qt_pa": "[{\"insert\":\"\\\"Writing is nature's way of letting you know how sloppy your thinking is.\\\" -Dick Guindon, via Leslie Lamport\"}]",
          "zItkb6": "[{\"insert\":\"Eliminate ambiguous words\",\"attributes\":{\"bold\":true}},{\"insert\":\". Actively avoid words which weaken your point (e.g. \\\"nearly\\\" instead of an exact percentage)\"}]",
          "KHjvBC": "[{\"insert\":\"The Pyramid Principles\",\"attributes\":{\"href\":\"https://medium.com/lessons-from-mckinsey/the-pyramid-principle-f0885dd3c5c7\"}}]",
          "PEaJVf": "[]",
          "2eSFYu": "[{\"insert\":\"Cut acronyms and jargon\",\"attributes\":{\"bold\":true}},{\"insert\":\". Aim to explain to a child. E.g. do not assume that someone understands what MR means. Instead, write out \\\"merge request.\\\"\"}]",
          "Rs8aAC": "[{\"insert\":\"The secret sauce of writing a good doc is to think clearly and thoroughly about your subject.\"}]",
